  "adaptations": [
    "Move selected C ABI adapters into the one Aphrody FFI crate",
    "Use root workspace dependencies and shared Rust Web libraries",
    "Keep historical symbol aliases only during consumer cutover",
    "Web job and embedding adapters reuse aphrody-ffi's existing process-wide Tokio runtime",
    "Chromium cookie adapter calls the locally imported shared profile parser; no credentials are imported",
    "Native Obscura HTTP adapter now has a nonblocking job submit symbol using the shared runtime",
    "The final source net.rs adapter now links local aphrody-x and aphrody-x-algorithm crates",
    "All 67 source Web ABI symbols and 65 shared signatures are present; Web ABI v4 is exported by the one cdylib",
    "Canonical network aliases are generated in web/net_aliases.rs while historical aliases remain for cutover"
  ],
